# Louie's Bakery
#
# This file is the authority on what the build needs. Kevin sets the real values in
# the Vercel dashboard; nothing here is ever a real value and no secret is ever
# written into this repo.
#
# The site runs with this file empty, which is the point of it being here: it says
# what is not yet wired as much as what is. With nothing set, the order form and the
# shipping checkout both still work, and both say plainly that no money has moved and
# nobody has been emailed.

# The origin this deployment actually serves from, used for absolute Open Graph
# image URLs. Vercel provides VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL automatically, so this
# is only needed to override it, for example on a custom pitch host.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://louies.vercel.app

# ── The shipping checkout on /cart ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stripe hosted Checkout. Server side only, never exposed to the browser. Set this
# and the cart takes the card on Stripe's own page; leave it unset and the same
# checkout emails the order to the bakery instead.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# Not read by anything yet: there is no webhook route. The bakery is emailed before
# the customer is sent to pay, which is what covers the gap. See api/checkout.
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── Order notifications ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where a pickup or shipping order lands. The bakery's own mailbox.
# ORDER_TO=

# Sending. Per glaze.md this should be SMTP through a mailbox the bakery already
# owns rather than a hosted API, with replyTo set to the customer.
# SMTP_HOST=
# SMTP_PORT=
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASS=
